      "description": "A group of students work on an innovative and entrepreneurial idea (a product, a venture or a service) which shows promise in bringing practical social benefits to the community. The idea should be feasible, sustainable, and promising in terms of improving social well-being.\n\nEach group should consist of students from diverse backgrounds. Students may form their own groups.\n\nStudents will work under the supervision of an instructor, who guides the students from the creation of an idea to the writing and presentation of a proposal and/or action plan. Performance throughout the work process is graded.\n\nAdvisory: For Final Year College students only.",
      "enrollment_requirement": "",
      "course_attributes": "STOT Course",
      "academic_career": "Undergraduate",
      "grading_basis": "Graded",
      "component": "Seminar",
      "campus": "Main Campus",
      "academic_group": "Wu Yee Sun College",
      "academic_org": "Wu Yee Sun College",
      "learning_outcomes": "Upon completing this course, the student will be able to:\n\n1. exercise own creativity in designing an innovative social venture\n\n2. form an opinion on the viability and effectiveness of a social venture\n\n3. work and communicate effectively in a team work environment\n\n4. write proposals/action plans and present them in verbal and written forms\n\n完成本科後, 學生將可:\n\n1. 透過設計創新的社會計劃去發揮創意\n\n2. 就社會計劃的可行性及有效性提出見解\n\n3. 在團隊環境中有效地溝通合作\n\n4. 撰寫計劃書/行動計劃, 並以口述和書面形式作報告",
